4805 total\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\n12:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_012JXj699oTbjhmQscB9XrG2\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"## Problem\\n\\nThe product cannot say what an item is waiting on. `attavo drive N` decides from the item's records and one read of the forge, and then either acts or prints one line into a log and exits: on #194 a concluded red check made it print \\\"stopped: forge checks not green\\\", exit 1, and write nothing, twice, while the operator screen showed a Launch button (#171). The decision is already a pure function (`drive_state` plus `read_forge_checks`); nothing exposes it without also acting on it, so every view derives its own answer and a refusal is an event nobody recorded instead of a level anybody can read.\\n\\nThis is R1 of the reconciler (`claude/reconciler-brief-2026-09-20.md`, rulings A and G, 2026-09-20): `attavo drive N --report` prints, as JSON against `schema/drive-report.schema.json`, the item's state, whose move it is (`yours`, `waits`, `acts`, `done`), and one sentence in the operator's words. It writes nothing, starts nothing, and never waits: it reads the forge once and does not call `poll_forge_checks`. No behaviour of `attavo drive N` without the flag changes. The states are the ones today's product can be in; attempt budgets, the breaker, and rulings arrive with R3 and R4 and add states then.\\n\\nThe stub under `stub/` is thin on purpose (the operator's ruling, 2026-09-20): it guesses the state from which files exist, satisfies the criteria, and fails eight of the thirteen tests in `tests/test_report.py`, which cover what it ignores (an expired approval, a record bound to an earlier approval or build, a live invocation inside and past the bound, counsel, a merged item). The build writes the report from the product's own functions; shipping the stub's `report.py` is not a build.\\n\\nA new reader must not wedge on a record that already exists (#194's `verify-01`): the report returns a state for every item this repository's records directory carries.\\n\\nRetires: #171 (a refusal is the report's current level, recomputed on every read, so there is nothing to record); any view's own derivation of what an item is waiting on (deleted by a screen item filed against this one once a release carries it).\\n\\n## Claims\\n\\n- attavo/report.py\\n- attavo/drive.py\\n- attavo/types.py\\n- attavo/cli.py\\n- schema/drive-report.schema.json\\n- tests/test_report.py\\n- tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\\n- tests/test_cli_help.py\\n\\n## Criteria\\n\\n- report-names-a-red-check-and-writes-nothing.sh: with a built item whose head carries a concluded red check, drive 1 --report exits 0, prints state blocked-on-checks, kind waits, stage verify, the check by name and conclusion, and a sentence naming the check and the head that says neither \\\"drive\\\" nor \\\"verify\\\"; HEAD, the working tree, and the item's records directory are the same before and after\\n- report-never-waits.sh: with a check still in_progress and the drive's poll bound set to 30 s, the report returns in under 10 s with state waiting-on-checks and the check named\\n- report-walks-an-item-and-names-whose-move-it-is.sh: across one item's life the report reads waiting-on-approval yours, next-build acts, owes-recovery acts naming build attempt 1 as died (and writes no record), stopped yours naming build-01, its class, and its filed issue, next-review acts, and ready-to-merge yours\\n- the-report-has-its-contract-and-its-tests.sh: schema/drive-report.schema.json closes its properties, requires every one, and enumerates the eleven states and four kinds; DriveReport mirrors it in tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py; tests/test_report.py carries its thirteen tests by name\\n=== criteria/report-names-a-red-check-and-writes-nothing.sh\\n#!/bin/sh\\nCONCLUSION=failure\\nset -e\\nhere=$(pwd)\\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\\ncp -R \\\"$here/tests/fixtures/build_valid/.\\\" \\\"$tmp/tenant\\\"\\ncd \\\"$tmp/tenant\\\"\\ngit init -q -b main .\\ngit config user.email fixture@attavo.invalid\\ngit config user.name \\\"fixture\\\"\\nprintf '\\\\n[forge]\\\\nchecks_command = \\\"printf '\\\"'\\\"'ci %s\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'\\\"'\\\"'\\\"\\\\n\\\\n[drive]\\\\nstall_after_s = 60\\\\n' \\\"$CONCLUSION\\\" >> attavo.toml\\ngit add -A\\ngit commit -q -m install\\ngit init -q --bare -b main \\\"$tmp/origin.git\\\"\\ngit remote add origin \\\"$tmp/origin.git\\\"\\ngit push -q origin HEAD:main\\ngit update-ref refs/remotes/origin/main \\\"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\"\\ngit symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD refs/remotes/origin/main\\nexport ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S=30 ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S=5\\nA=\\\"python3 $here/bin/attavo\\\"\\nsnapshot() { printf '%s\\\\n%s\\\\n%s\\\\n' \\\"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\" \\\"$(git status --porcelain)\\\" \\\"$(ls records/1 2>/dev/null)\\\"; }\\n$A spec-gate 1 >/dev/null\\n$A approve 1 --by alice >/dev/null\\n$A drive 1 >/dev/null\\nbefore=$(snapshot)\\n$A drive 1 --report > \\\"$tmp/report.json\\\"\\ntest \\\"$(snapshot)\\\" = \\\"$before\\\"\\npython3 - \\\"$(git rev-parse --short=7 HEAD)\\\" \\\"$tmp/report.json\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport json, sys\\nr = json.load(open(sys.argv[2]))\\nassert (r[\\\"state\\\"], r[\\\"kind\\\"], r[\\\"stage\\\"]) == (\\\"blocked-on-checks\\\", \\\"waits\\\", \\\"verify\\\"), r\\nassert r[\\\"checks\\\"] == [{\\\"name\\\": \\\"ci\\\", \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"failure\\\"}], r\\nassert \\\"ci failure\\\" in r[\\\"says\\\"] and sys.argv[1] in r[\\\"says\\\"], r\\nassert \\\"drive\\\" not in r[\\\"says\\\"].lower() and \\\"verify\\\" not in r[\\\"says\\\"].lower(), r\\nPY\\ntest -z \\\"$(ls records/1 | grep '^verify-')\\\"\\ncd \\\"$here\\\"\\nrm -rf \\\"$tmp\\\"\\n=== criteria/report-never-waits.sh\\n#!/bin/sh\\nCONCLUSION=in_progress\\nset -e\\nhere=$(pwd)\\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\\ncp -R \\\"$here/tests/fixtures/build_valid/.\\\" \\\"$tmp/tenant\\\"\\ncd \\\"$tmp/tenant\\\"\\ngit init -q -b main .\\ngit config user.email fixture@attavo.invalid\\ngit config user.name \\\"fixture\\\"\\nprintf '\\\\n[forge]\\\\nchecks_command = \\\"printf '\\\"'\\\"'ci %s\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'\\\"'\\\"'\\\"\\\\n\\\\n[drive]\\\\nstall_after_s = 60\\\\n' \\\"$CONCLUSION\\\" >> attavo.toml\\ngit add -A\\ngit commit -q -m install\\ngit init -q --bare -b main \\\"$tmp/origin.git\\\"\\ngit remote add origin \\\"$tmp/origin.git\\\"\\ngit push -q origin HEAD:main\\ngit update-ref refs/remotes/origin/main \\\"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\"\\ngit symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD refs/remotes/origin/main\\nexport ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S=30 ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S=5\\nA=\\\"python3 $here/bin/attavo\\\"\\nsnapshot() { printf '%s\\\\n%s\\\\n%s\\\\n' \\\"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\" \\\"$(git status --porcelain)\\\" \\\"$(ls records/1 2>/dev/null)\\\"; }\\n$A spec-gate 1 >/dev/null\\n$A approve 1 --by alice >/dev/null\\n$A drive 1 >/dev/null\\nstarted=$(date +%s)\\n$A drive 1 --report > \\\"$tmp/report.json\\\"\\ntest $(( $(date +%s) - started )) -lt 10\\npython3 - \\\"$tmp/report.json\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport json, sys\\nr = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))\\nassert (r[\\\"state\\\"], r[\\\"kind\\\"]) == (\\\"waiting-on-checks\\\", \\\"waits\\\"), r\\nassert \\\"ci in_progress\\\" in r[\\\"says\\\"], r\\nPY\\ncd \\\"$here\\\"\\nrm -rf \\\"$tmp\\\"\\n=== criteria/report-walks-an-item-and-names-whose-move-it-is.sh\\n#!/bin/sh\\nCONCLUSION=success\\nset -e\\nhere=$(pwd)\\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\\ncp -R \\\"$here/tests/fixtures/build_valid/.\\\" \\\"$tmp/tenant\\\"\\ncd \\\"$tmp/tenant\\\"\\ngit init -q -b main .\\ngit config user.email fixture@attavo.invalid\\ngit config user.name \\\"fixture\\\"\\nprintf '\\\\n[forge]\\\\nchecks_command = \\\"printf '\\\"'\\\"'ci %s\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'\\\"'\\\"'\\\"\\\\n\\\\n[drive]\\\\nstall_after_s = 60\\\\n' \\\"$CONCLUSION\\\" >> attavo.toml\\ngit add -A\\ngit commit -q -m install\\ngit init -q --bare -b main \\\"$tmp/origin.git\\\"\\ngit remote add origin \\\"$tmp/origin.git\\\"\\ngit push -q origin HEAD:main\\ngit update-ref refs/remotes/origin/main \\\"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\"\\ngit symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD refs/remotes/origin/main\\nexport ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S=30 ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S=5\\nA=\\\"python3 $here/bin/attavo\\\"\\nsnapshot() { printf '%s\\\\n%s\\\\n%s\\\\n' \\\"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\" \\\"$(git status --porcelain)\\\" \\\"$(ls records/1 2>/dev/null)\\\"; }\\nstate() { $A drive 1 --report | python3 -c 'import json,sys; r=json.load(sys.stdin); print(r[\\\"state\\\"], r[\\\"kind\\\"])'; }\\n$A spec-gate 1 >/dev/null\\ntest \\\"$(state)\\\" = \\\"waiting-on-approval yours\\\"\\n$A approve 1 --by alice >/dev/null\\ntest \\\"$(state)\\\" = \\\"next-build acts\\\"\\nsleep 0 &\\ndead=$!\\nwait \\\"$dead\\\"\\npython3 - records/1/build-01.started \\\"$dead\\\" \\\"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport json, socket, sys\\njson.dump({\\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-09-17T13:16:08Z\\\", \\\"host\\\": socket.gethostname(), \\\"pid\\\": int(sys.argv[2]),\\n           \\\"sha\\\": sys.argv[3], \\\"product_version\\\": \\\"fixture\\\"}, open(sys.argv[1], \\\"w\\\"))\\nPY\\ngit add records\\ngit commit -q -m \\\"invocation marker for item 1\\\"\\nbefore=$(snapshot)\\n$A drive 1 --report > \\\"$tmp/owes.json\\\"\\ntest \\\"$(snapshot)\\\" = \\\"$before\\\"\\npython3 - \\\"$tmp/owes.json\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport json, sys\\nr = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))\\nassert (r[\\\"state\\\"], r[\\\"kind\\\"], r[\\\"stage\\\"], r[\\\"attempt\\\"], r[\\\"stop_class\\\"]) == (\\\"owes-recovery\\\", \\\"acts\\\", \\\"build\\\", 1, \\\"died\\\"), r\\nPY\\n$A drive --recover 1 >/dev/null\\nprintf 'https://example.invalid/issues/9\\\\n' > records/1/build-01.filed\\ngit add records\\ngit commit -q -m \\\"the stop is filed\\\"\\n$A drive 1 --report > \\\"$tmp/stopped.json\\\"\\npython3 - \\\"$tmp/stopped.json\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport json, sys\\nr = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))\\nassert (r[\\\"state\\\"], r[\\\"kind\\\"], r[\\\"record\\\"], r[\\\"stop_class\\\"], r[\\\"filed\\\"]) == (\\\"stopped\\\", \\\"yours\\\", \\\"build-01\\\", \\\"died\\\", \\\"https://example.invalid/issues/9\\\"), r\\nPY\\n$A drive 1 >/dev/null\\ntest \\\"$(state)\\\" = \\\"next-review acts\\\"\\n$A drive 1 >/dev/null\\ntest \\\"$(state)\\\" = \\\"ready-to-merge yours\\\"\\ncd \\\"$here\\\"\\nrm -rf \\\"$tmp\\\"\\n=== criteria/the-report-has-its-contract-and-its-tests.sh\\n#!/bin/sh\\nset -e\\npython3 - <<'PY'\\nimport json\\ns = json.load(open(\\\"schema/drive-report.schema.json\\\"))\\nassert s[\\\"additionalProperties\\\"] is False and set(s[\\\"required\\\"]) == set(s[\\\"properties\\\"]), s[\\\"required\\\"]\\nfor state in (\\\"waiting-on-approval\\\", \\\"running\\\", \\\"owes-recovery\\\", \\\"stopped\\\", \\\"next-build\\\", \\\"waiting-on-checks\\\",\\n              \\\"blocked-on-checks\\\", \\\"next-review\\\", \\\"ready-to-merge\\\", \\\"merged\\\", \\\"refused\\\"):\\n    assert state in s[\\\"properties\\\"][\\\"state\\\"][\\\"enum\\\"], state\\nassert s[\\\"properties\\\"][\\\"kind\\\"][\\\"enum\\\"] == [\\\"yours\\\", \\\"waits\\\", \\\"acts\\\", \\\"done\\\"]\\nPY\\ngrep -q '\\\"DriveReport\\\": \\\"drive-report.schema.json\\\"' tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\\nfor t in test_report_names_a_red_check_and_the_head_and_writes_nothing test_report_never_waits_on_a_check_that_is_still_running test_report_walks_an_item_from_approval_to_ready test_report_says_what_recovery_would_record_for_a_dead_invocation test_report_names_the_stopped_record_its_class_its_counsel_and_its_issue test_report_reads_an_expired_approval_as_yours_and_says_why test_report_reads_a_live_invocation_inside_the_bound_as_running test_report_reads_a_live_invocation_past_the_bound_as_hung_and_ends_nothing test_report_reads_a_review_of_an_earlier_build_as_review_next test_report_does_not_read_a_failed_build_of_an_earlier_approval_as_stopped test_report_names_the_counsel_record_that_read_the_stop test_report_reads_a_merged_item_as_merged test_report_reads_every_item_this_repository_carries\\ndo\\n  grep -q \\\"^def $t(\\\" tests/test_report.py\\ndone\\nattavo\\nschema\\ntests\\n\\nstub/attavo:\\ndrive.py\\nreport.py\\ntypes.py\\n\\nstub/schema:\\ndrive-report.schema.json\\n\\nstub/tests:\\ntest_report.py\\ntest_types_mirror_schemas.py\\n{\\n  \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-09-20T17:28:48Z\\\",\\n  \\\"host\\\": \\\"Davids-MacBook-Pro.local\\\",\\n  \\\"pid\\\": 20757,\\n  \\\"sha\\\": \\\"d1fd30c7121d2f4d21037851d53efb5e3c2bf174\\\",\\n  \\\"product_version\\\": \\\"v0.26.0-43-g1cb8af3\\\"\\n}\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"8de61c42-af71-4210-8ec4-d6e4cd3c023f\",\"uuid\":\"4634df54-ecee-4d70-973b-b8daa893dfd8\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-20T17:32:53.540Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"## Problem\\n\\nThe product cannot say what an item is waiting on. `attavo drive N` decides from the item's records and one read of the forge, and then either acts or prints one line into a log and exits: on #194 a concluded red check made it print \\\"stopped: forge checks not green\\\", exit 1, and write nothing, twice, while the operator screen showed a Launch button (#171). The decision is already a pure function (`drive_state` plus `read_forge_checks`); nothing exposes it without also acting on it, so every view derives its own answer and a refusal is an event nobody recorded instead of a level anybody can read.\\n\\nThis is R1 of the reconciler (`claude/reconciler-brief-2026-09-20.md`, rulings A and G, 2026-09-20): `attavo drive N --report` prints, as JSON against `schema/drive-report.schema.json`, the item's state, whose move it is (`yours`, `waits`, `acts`, `done`), and one sentence in the operator's words. It writes nothing, starts nothing, and never waits: it reads the forge once and does not call `poll_forge_checks`. No behaviour of `attavo drive N` without the flag changes. The states are the ones today's product can be in; attempt budgets, the breaker, and rulings arrive with R3 and R4 and add states then.\\n\\nThe stub under `stub/` is thin on purpose (the operator's ruling, 2026-09-20): it guesses the state from which files exist, satisfies the criteria, and fails eight of the thirteen tests in `tests/test_report.py`, which cover what it ignores (an expired approval, a record bound to an earlier approval or build, a live invocation inside and past the bound, counsel, a merged item). The build writes the report from the product's own functions; shipping the stub's `report.py` is not a build.\\n\\nA new reader must not wedge on a record that already exists (#194's `verify-01`): the report returns a state for every item this repository's records directory carries.\\n\\nRetires: #171 (a refusal is the report's current level, recomputed on every read, so there is nothing to record); any view's own derivation of what an item is waiting on (deleted by a screen item filed against this one once a release carries it).\\n\\n## Claims\\n\\n- attavo/report.py\\n- attavo/drive.py\\n- attavo/types.py\\n- attavo/cli.py\\n- schema/drive-report.schema.json\\n- tests/test_report.py\\n- tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\\n- tests/test_cli_help.py\\n\\n## Criteria\\n\\n- report-names-a-red-check-and-writes-nothing.sh: with a built item whose head carries a concluded red check, drive 1 --report exits 0, prints state blocked-on-checks, kind waits, stage verify, the check by name and conclusion, and a sentence naming the check and the head that says neither \\\"drive\\\" nor \\\"verify\\\"; HEAD, the working tree, and the item's records directory are the same before and after\\n- report-never-waits.sh: with a check still in_progress and the drive's poll bound set to 30 s, the report returns in under 10 s with state waiting-on-checks and the check named\\n- report-walks-an-item-and-names-whose-move-it-is.sh: across one item's life the report reads waiting-on-approval yours, next-build acts, owes-recovery acts naming build attempt 1 as died (and writes no record), stopped yours naming build-01, its class, and its filed issue, next-review acts, and ready-to-merge yours\\n- the-report-has-its-contract-and-its-tests.sh: schema/drive-report.schema.json closes its properties, requires every one, and enumerates the eleven states and four kinds; DriveReport mirrors it in tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py; tests/test_report.py carries its thirteen tests by name\\n=== criteria/report-names-a-red-check-and-writes-nothing.sh\\n#!/bin/sh\\nCONCLUSION=failure\\nset -e\\nhere=$(pwd)\\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\\ncp -R \\\"$here/tests/fixtures/build_valid/.\\\" \\\"$tmp/tenant\\\"\\ncd \\\"$tmp/tenant\\\"\\ngit init -q -b main .\\ngit config user.email fixture@attavo.invalid\\ngit config user.name \\\"fixture\\\"\\nprintf '\\\\n[forge]\\\\nchecks_command = \\\"printf '\\\"'\\\"'ci %s\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'\\\"'\\\"'\\\"\\\\n\\\\n[drive]\\\\nstall_after_s = 60\\\\n' \\\"$CONCLUSION\\\" >> attavo.toml\\ngit add -A\\ngit commit -q -m install\\ngit init -q --bare -b main \\\"$tmp/origin.git\\\"\\ngit remote add origin \\\"$tmp/origin.git\\\"\\ngit push -q origin HEAD:main\\ngit update-ref refs/remotes/origin/main \\\"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\"\\ngit symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD refs/remotes/origin/main\\nexport ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S=30 ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S=5\\nA=\\\"python3 $here/bin/attavo\\\"\\nsnapshot() { printf '%s\\\\n%s\\\\n%s\\\\n' \\\"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\" \\\"$(git status --porcelain)\\\" \\\"$(ls records/1 2>/dev/null)\\\"; }\\n$A spec-gate 1 >/dev/null\\n$A approve 1 --by alice >/dev/null\\n$A drive 1 >/dev/null\\nbefore=$(snapshot)\\n$A drive 1 --report > \\\"$tmp/report.json\\\"\\ntest \\\"$(snapshot)\\\" = \\\"$before\\\"\\npython3 - \\\"$(git rev-parse --short=7 HEAD)\\\" \\\"$tmp/report.json\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport json, sys\\nr = json.load(open(sys.argv[2]))\\nassert (r[\\\"state\\\"], r[\\\"kind\\\"], r[\\\"stage\\\"]) == (\\\"blocked-on-checks\\\", \\\"waits\\\", \\\"verify\\\"), r\\nassert r[\\\"checks\\\"] == [{\\\"name\\\": \\\"ci\\\", \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"failure\\\"}], r\\nassert \\\"ci failure\\\" in r[\\\"says\\\"] and sys.argv[1] in r[\\\"says\\\"], r\\nassert \\\"drive\\\" not in r[\\\"says\\\"].lower() and \\\"verify\\\" not in r[\\\"says\\\"].lower(), r\\nPY\\ntest -z \\\"$(ls records/1 | grep '^veri","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/davidbean/.claude/projects/-Users-davidbean-Projects-attavo-worktree-206/53e9fb7a-7be9-4016-bba8-bc8cef16ea31/tool-results/b5ofoq4o7.txt","persistedOutputSize":128277}}
